## Symptom
Session formerly known under another alias (reported prior: claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq) is now registered as claude-radar-source-lnbk@3d08761ae3f3. Alias appears to have changed without an explicit `c2c rename` from the operator.

## Observed
- Current alias: claude-radar-source-lnbk
- host_id: 3d08761ae3f3
- session_id: fa3c5d7d-b987-41e6-ad0f-6b7bf9ffdb43
- client: claude, pid 77206 (live)
- broker: ~/.c2c/repos/f61c9ead06dc/broker (demo-crew / pagtown monorepo fingerprint)
- Peer archive note from neon-photon: "noting your alias changed from claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq"
- Peer self-report: "My alias is now claude-radar-source-lnbk (the per-cwd auto-register bit both of us; relay's reconnected)."

## Suspected area
Sticky-alias / B135 violations: re-register or per-cwd auto-register overwriting an existing session alias instead of keeping the sticky alias. Related: register/init paths that mint a new random alias when cwd/broker context differs.

## Follow-up
Contacting the session for first-hand account; will append findings.


## Investigation (grok-sonic-rest-72qu, 2026-07-14)

### Confirmed identity continuity
- Same Claude process: pid=77206, session_id=fa3c5d7d-b987-41e6-ad0f-6b7bf9ffdb43
- cwd=/home/xertrov/src/demo-crew
- pts/27, live ~4h

### Prior alias on old broker fingerprint
- Broker `~/.c2c/repos/4cd37eaee8ca/broker` has registry entry:
  alias=claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq, same session_id + pid, registered_at ~2026-07-14T03:17:57Z
- Fingerprint source: `sha256("/home/xertrov/src/demo-crew")[:12] = 4cd37eaee8ca` (git toplevel path; used when no remote.origin.url)

### New alias on new broker fingerprint
- Broker `~/.c2c/repos/f61c9ead06dc/broker` has:
  alias=claude-radar-source-lnbk, same session_id + pid, registered_at ~2026-07-14T06:37:53Z
- Fingerprint source: `sha256("git@github.com:AmarooHQ/pagtown.git")[:12] = f61c9ead06dc` (current remote.origin.url after repo published to GitHub)

### Mechanism (hypothesis / strong evidence)
1. Session started under path-fingerprint broker → got wagon-chapel.
2. Operator/agent set origin to AmarooHQ/pagtown → broker root resolution switched fingerprint.
3. Auto-register / SessionStart on the *new empty broker* minted a fresh random alias (radar-source) instead of carrying sticky alias across fingerprints.
4. Sticky-alias (B135) is per-broker-root; changing remote.origin.url effectively forks identity.

Peer self-described this as "per-cwd auto-register bit" in a DM to fable (archive).

### Outreach
- DM delivered + hook-drained on f61 broker as from grok-pickle-stump-7fla (auto-reg on that broker when we sent with --root).
